# Normalize line endings to LF in the working tree.
#
# The application files are bind-mounted into Linux containers. A shell
# script checked out with CRLF line endings fails to exec with
# "exec /app/scripts/network_chaos.sh: no such file or directory" because the
# kernel treats the CR as part of the "#!" interpreter path. Forcing LF keeps
# the scripts runnable on Windows hosts as well as Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf
